For $ds^2=4x^2dx^2$, the flat coordinate is $\Phi(x)=x^2$. The intrinsic midpoint of $2$ and $1$ has square $5/2$. The Euler endpoint $3/2$ has square $9/4$, so the points differ.
</details>

